{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 18 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the store/snapshot/io subsystem (_store, _snapshot, _io) as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. RP-04 is not complete while these sit below the seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nAffected SOURCE files: `src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py`, `_snapshot/git_fetch.py`, `_snapshot/janitor.py`, `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`, `_store/ensures.py`, `_store/env_identity.py`, `_store/hlc.py`, `_store/lock.py`, `_store/project_ensures.py`, `_store/push.py`; plus `src/rebar/config.py` (may add/reuse owned resolvers) and `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the 18 rows).\n\nAffected TEST consumers (updated in-scope — they set the cut env vars directly and drive the affected helpers, so cutting the reads changes how they inject): `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py` (REBAR_GATE_* `from_env`), `tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py` + `tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py` (REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_*), `tests/unit/test_repo_snapshot.py` + `test_snapshot_cache.py` + `test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py` + `test_snapshot_docs.py` (REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR / snapshot knobs), `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py` (REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES), and any test setting `REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY` that drives `_store/env_identity.py`.\n\n## Outcome\nEach of the 18 reads is dispositioned by the decision rule into exactly one treatment and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths, no path-glob exception. The regression suites (below) stay green (affected `tests/unit` consumers updated where the injection path changed). Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded (with rationale) as a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; majority).** A read whose value is composed config (a typed `Config` field, a `[snapshot]`/`sync`/`ensure`/`jira` key, or `load_config()`) is CUT: threaded from an owned `config.py` resolver (reuse landed `compose_config()`, or a targeted resolver) instead of ambient `os.environ`/`load_config` below the seam. The ambient read no longer exists. This changes below-seam helper signatures to RECEIVE the value, so the `tests/unit` consumers above inject via the new signature/typed config and run in the regression suite.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed config — genuine test-only injection, subsystem kill-switch, or subprocess/protocol env-control — stays with a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. CAPPED at the 3 enumerated logical reads below; the gate flags each accessed LINE separately, so those 3 reads = exactly **5 marked lines**. No other listed read may be marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (3 reads = 5 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `_store/hlc.py` L61 `REBAR_HLC` — subsystem kill-switch (`REBAR_HLC=0` reverts HLC to raw `physical_now()`). 1 line.\n2. `_store/hlc.py` L71 `REBAR_HLC_NOW` — test-only injection of the physical clock source (skewed-clock tests). 1 line.\n3. `_io/import_ndjson.py` L216/L217/L395 `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` — subprocess/protocol env-control: L216 reads prior value, L217 sets `=off` for child processes, L395 restores. Not composed config. 3 lines.\n\nAll 15 other reads (3 `load_config()`; `REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_*` x3; `REBAR_GATE_*` x6 incl. janitor dynamic `os.environ.get`; `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`; `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`; `REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY`) are treatment (a).\n\n## Plan\n1. Cut the 15 composed-config reads: thread each from an owned `config.py` resolver (reuse `compose_config()`; add a narrow resolver only where a typed value is cleaner), changing below-seam helper signatures to RECEIVE the value. Preserve exact semantics (env>config-table>default for the `[snapshot]` knobs; clamping for `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`).\n2. Update the affected `tests/unit` consumers to inject via the new signature/typed config rather than the now-cut env var; keep their assertions.\n3. Mark the 3 owned-in-place reads (5 lines) with `# read-via:` markers naming the category; no other markers.\n4. Remove the 18 rows from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`.\n5. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the regression set below; keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding containing any listed source path; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries whose `path` is a listed source file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across the listed source files total exactly 5, confined to `_store/hlc.py` (2) and `_io/import_ndjson.py` (3) — every other listed file has 0 — so blanket-marking cannot substitute for cutting. RED now (rows present + reads below seam + no markers).\nRegression suites kept green: `tests/interfaces/store`, `tests/integration` store/snapshot, AND the affected `tests/unit` suites (test_snapshot_janitor, test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4, test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e, test_repo_snapshot, test_snapshot_cache, test_snapshot_blobless_747f, test_snapshot_docs, test_lock_retry_zebrafish). Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after equal except recorded deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored format changes. Cut-to-seam is pure routing/threading; the 5 marked lines are inline annotations on 3 non-config env-control reads. Rollback = revert the single change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the seam in the 10 listed source files: each read is cut-to-seam (15) or one of the 3 enumerated owned-in-place reads (5 marked lines) with a `# read-via:` category rationale; no other read marked.\n- [ ] The 18 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out test incl. its marker-total==5 / per-file-placement check).\n- [ ] The regression suites in Testing pass after the cutover (affected `tests/unit` consumers updated only where the injection path changed); operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded with rationale as a comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787105656782319001,"uuid":"7ba03e33-1d09-4c47-ae2c-ca5fa6501871"}